    "outlook": "The Indian market saw a positive close for NIFTY and SENSEX, primarily propelled by a strong performance in the IT sector. While FIIs were net sellers, significant buying from DIIs provided crucial support, maintaining a positive market breadth. Investors should watch for continued momentum in IT and the resilience of domestic flows, despite minor dips in banking and other defensive sectors.",
    "keyTakeaways": [
      "NIFTY 50 (+0.35%) and SENSEX (+0.43%) closed higher, driven by select sectors.",
      "NIFTY IT surged +3.51%, with top gainers like TCS, TechM, and Infy leading the rally.",
      "FIIs were net sellers (-298.26cr), while DIIs provided strong buying support (+4977.17cr).",
      "Market breadth was positive with 31 advances against 26 declines.",
      "NIFTY BANK saw a marginal dip of -0.02%, indicating a mixed performance among financial stocks.",
      "VIX remained low at 10.68, suggesting reduced market volatility."
